Bits.Description:
Maximum payload. Shows the largest number of data bytes per frame that this build can store and transmit (PARA_CANFD_DATA_MAX); longer received frames are still checked and acknowledged but only the first bytes are kept.

Usage: read before software chooses the element sizes in cfd_esz.

Values:
0x0 8 bytes;
0x1 12 bytes;
0x2 16 bytes;
0x3 20 bytes;
0x4 24 bytes;
0x5 32 bytes;
0x6 48 bytes;
0x7 64 bytes.

Unit: bytes.

Limits: An element size above this value is clamped..

Safety level. Shows the value of PARA_CANFD_SAF_LEVEL of this build.

Usage: read by the safety software to know which mechanisms the hardware can provide.

Values:
0x0 no safety level;
0x1 basic;
0x2 full;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: The value is 0 to 2..

Bus activity. Shows what the protocol engine does at the moment.

Usage: software reads it; hardware updates it, the value is a snapshot from the CAN domain.

Values:
0x0 synchronizing to the bus;
0x1 idle;
0x2 receiving;
0x3 transmitting.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Last error code of the data phase of FD frames.

Usage: software reads it; hardware updates it, the value is a snapshot from the CAN domain.

Values:
0x0 no error;
0x1 stuff error;
0x2 form error;
0x3 acknowledge error;
0x4 bit1 error;
0x5 bit0 error;
0x6 CRC error;
0x7 no change.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Last error code of the arbitration phase and of Classic frames.

Usage: software reads it; hardware updates it, the value is a snapshot from the CAN domain.

Values:
0x0 no error;
0x1 stuff error;
0x2 form error;
0x3 acknowledge error;
0x4 bit1 error;
0x5 bit0 error;
0x6 CRC error;
0x7 no change.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Accept non-matching frames extended. Action for an extended-format frame that matches no filter element.

Usage: software writes it only while INIT = 1 and CCE = 1; a write in another state is ignored.

Values:
0x0 accept into Rx FIFO 0;
0x1 accept into Rx FIFO 1;
0x2 reject;
0x3 reject.

Unit: none.

Limits: Use 0x1 only when Rx FIFO 1 is built..

Accept non-matching frames standard. Action for a base-format frame that matches no filter element.

Usage: software writes it only while INIT = 1 and CCE = 1; a write in another state is ignored.

Values:
0x0 accept into Rx FIFO 0;
0x1 accept into Rx FIFO 1;
0x2 reject;
0x3 reject.

Unit: none.

Limits: Use 0x1 only when Rx FIFO 1 is built..

Tx buffer data field size. Number of data bytes of one Tx element; the DLC of the frame must not need more.

Usage: software writes it only while INIT = 1 and CCE = 1; a write in another state is ignored.

Values:
0x0 8 data bytes;
0x1 12 data bytes;
0x2 16 data bytes;
0x3 20 data bytes;
0x4 24 data bytes;
0x5 32 data bytes;
0x6 48 data bytes;
0x7 64 data bytes.

Unit: bytes.

Limits: Use 0x7 for 64-byte FD frames..

Rx buffer data field size. Number of data bytes of one dedicated buffer element; a longer frame is stored cut.

Usage: software writes it only while INIT = 1 and CCE = 1; a write in another state is ignored.

Values:
0x0 8 data bytes;
0x1 12 data bytes;
0x2 16 data bytes;
0x3 20 data bytes;
0x4 24 data bytes;
0x5 32 data bytes;
0x6 48 data bytes;
0x7 64 data bytes.

Unit: bytes.

Limits: Use 0x7 for 64-byte FD frames..

Rx FIFO 1 data field size. Number of data bytes of one element; a longer frame is stored cut.

Usage: software writes it only while INIT = 1 and CCE = 1; a write in another state is ignored.

Values:
0x0 8 data bytes;
0x1 12 data bytes;
0x2 16 data bytes;
0x3 20 data bytes;
0x4 24 data bytes;
0x5 32 data bytes;
0x6 48 data bytes;
0x7 64 data bytes.

Unit: bytes.

Limits: Use 0x7 for 64-byte FD frames..

Rx FIFO 0 data field size. Number of data bytes of one element; a longer frame is stored cut.

Usage: software writes it only while INIT = 1 and CCE = 1; a write in another state is ignored.

Values:
0x0 8 data bytes;
0x1 12 data bytes;
0x2 16 data bytes;
0x3 20 data bytes;
0x4 24 data bytes;
0x5 32 data bytes;
0x6 48 data bytes;
0x7 64 data bytes.

Unit: bytes.

Limits: Use 0x7 for 64-byte FD frames..

Timestamp source. Selects what runs the timestamp counter.

Usage: software writes it only while INIT = 1 and CCE = 1; a write in another state is ignored.

Values:
0x0 counter stopped, timestamps are zero;
0x1 internal counter;
0x2 external timestamp vector i_ts_ext;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: The value 0x2 needs ts_ext_en of cfd_feat0..

Timeout select. Chooses what restarts the counter.

Usage: software writes it with the counter off.

Values:
0x0 continuous;
0x1 restart by Rx FIFO 0;
0x2 restart by the Tx event FIFO;
0x3 restart by Rx FIFO 1.

Unit: none.

Limits: The values 0x1 to 0x3 need the FIFO in question to be built..

TT operation mode. Selects event-driven or time-triggered communication.

Usage: software writes it only while INIT = 1 and CCE = 1; a write in another state is ignored; the TT registers are copied to the CAN domain with the configuration; it is the last step of the TT setup.

Values:
0x0 event-driven CAN communication (reset value);
0x1 TT configuration;
0x2 strictly time-triggered operation;
0x3 event-synchronised time-triggered operation.

Unit: none.

Limits: The values 0x1 to 0x3 need tt_en of cfd_feat0; FD operation (fdoe) is ignored in the values 0x2 and 0x3..

TT error level. The severity of the most serious TT error.

Usage: software reads it; hardware updates it, the value is a snapshot from the CAN domain.

Values:
0x0 no error;
0x1 warning;
0x2 error;
0x3 fatal error.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Master state. Shows the role of the node.

Usage: software reads it; hardware updates it, the value is a snapshot from the CAN domain.

Values:
0x0 time slave or master off;
0x1 current time master;
0x2 backup time master;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Synchronization state. Shows whether the node is in step with the schedule.

Usage: software reads it; hardware updates it, the value is a snapshot from the CAN domain.

Values:
0x0 out of synchronisation;
0x1 synchronising (one reference message seen);
0x2 in schedule;
0x3 in gap.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Time mark source. Selects the time that is compared with the time mark.

Usage: software writes it at any time; the global time needs level 2.

Values:
0x0 cycle time;
0x1 local time;
0x2 global time;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Stop-watch source. Selects the time that i_tt_swatch_trig captures.

Usage: software writes it at any time.

Values:
0x0 stop-watch off;
0x1 local time;
0x2 cycle time;
0x3 global time.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.
